\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338006/field-1" "q-338006/field-2" "q-338006/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90930e15-0827-5e0b-82cf-98263fc756d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338006"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338087/field-1/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "d6945ac5-5b14-50da-ba3a-e02a47e25203" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338087/field-1/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer/id #uuid "ace65b49-4419-5718-8126-2e2057f2ea39" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338087/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "67d1ac7f-49ac-53f3-b2b5-97f2c1011a54" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338087/field-1/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-338087/field-1/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" "q-338087/field-1/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338087/field-2/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer/id #uuid "694551d3-1a8a-5eb8-8650-df6f36571d69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338087/field-2/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "6422240b-f86a-5471-9ed1-f86e721a8810" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338087/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "98980f04-b0e7-5aa8-9878-0137594db6fd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338087/field-2/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-338087/field-2/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" "q-338087/field-2/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338087/field-3/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "119ad110-b97d-506f-b2c5-faffbc0a0477" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338087/field-3/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer/id #uuid "908f158f-7201-5387-a9e3-fdc01404665a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338087/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "249e9ea1-b271-5661-a0ca-c5a0da6cef5b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-338087/field-3/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-338087/field-3/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" "q-338087/field-3/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338087" :question/id #uuid "916dc27d-5ed7-5589-9d6c-93214bdd310b" :question/math-academy-id "q-338087" :question/problem "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.$\\,$ The equation $\\,\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+(x-2){y}^{′}+y=0$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,({x}^{2}+1){y}^{″}-4x{y}^{′}+3y=0$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,y+9=0$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+(x-2){y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+1){y}^{″}-4x{y}^{′}+3y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,y+9=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,y=-9.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-9,$ which is different from zero." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338087/field-1" "q-338087/field-2" "q-338087/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90930e15-0827-5e0b-82cf-98263fc756d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338087"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130994/selection/4d87c7d394e522be584324a615a28e65c003869c370a139ef05e19ffaa2811fd" :answer/id #uuid "01a7edac-65b4-55b2-b841-321337998ab1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130994/selection/dd7a78982f773b2fe761b627971e81b141ea5d3c2222f21d8ad58798103130ad" :answer/id #uuid "953b859e-e79c-5a28-a1ab-b3d691bb31d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+3y=\\frac{x}{x-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130994/selection/3b3340a6d2fa65ab5d6681eb928480c765cd69ac971d45bc7357158115391cf5" :answer/id #uuid "4d1873d6-cb10-583f-b48d-fa4e9dd2110b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-2){y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+3y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130994/selection/c44de5d653eff40fa0b508b1e35a23d56305c559a4de92fe6566854288f4834d" :answer/id #uuid "f9d1e1af-11f4-59bb-8e93-18b2c0721be7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+3y=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130994/selection/c51268a3c16819df68e2531fc1a9d1d61c05688dfde125012a7797c8386d14b7" :answer/id #uuid "580c7842-e8a1-5375-b0cb-682d9253df09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+3y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130994/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd5e249f-97c8-5674-b08e-67fec4f0ba87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130994/selection/3b3340a6d2fa65ab5d6681eb928480c765cd69ac971d45bc7357158115391cf5" :answer-field/choices ["q-130994/selection/4d87c7d394e522be584324a615a28e65c003869c370a139ef05e19ffaa2811fd" "q-130994/selection/dd7a78982f773b2fe761b627971e81b141ea5d3c2222f21d8ad58798103130ad" "q-130994/selection/3b3340a6d2fa65ab5d6681eb928480c765cd69ac971d45bc7357158115391cf5" "q-130994/selection/c44de5d653eff40fa0b508b1e35a23d56305c559a4de92fe6566854288f4834d" "q-130994/selection/c51268a3c16819df68e2531fc1a9d1d61c05688dfde125012a7797c8386d14b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130994" :question/id #uuid "ab9d13a9-1976-536d-bfec-9829d43ce57a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130994" :question/problem "For the differential equation $(x-2){y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+3y=x,$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n(x-2){y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+3y=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130994/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66ec8603-ae96-5212-88e1-4571d7face6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130994"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130996/selection/1ef83273bf8719dd6db6c440e0c0e3d9d136bdf66ea3f4f6db78210e7aebfed3" :answer/id #uuid "74f85049-fd80-5f31-8912-242efdd76111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{y}^{″}+(x+1){y}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130996/selection/b073349d38b9807332f930743cc5ce844707509ff0ef625bc61514b80924c235" :answer/id #uuid "d5594ba2-072f-5ae5-bd34-3bc5718aada8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-y={e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130996/selection/1583ad1c235afa6d610408beccb6b8d503778c5e2df64a981a8ce130972de08d" :answer/id #uuid "f707b7b8-ab16-55a2-8396-6c0d6a5362d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{y}^{″}+(x+1){y}^{′}-y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130996/selection/491523a3d62207c0b47e9c957e7ca9e1c64ef62097cde0d6985d20945c91f2da" :answer/id #uuid "2cbdae09-107a-5ccc-9c79-1d465c9a5378" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}-y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130996/selection/b34d76d1c0f1ddc92081e1f2abec37a147c832448b1ac795ea8045da7d2b1097" :answer/id #uuid "1184f437-b848-5bf7-a89a-2ac02dd56283" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+\\frac{x+1}{x}{y}^{′}-y={e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130996/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf05e959-ea8c-5cf6-bfd2-0d4d678cf741" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130996/selection/1583ad1c235afa6d610408beccb6b8d503778c5e2df64a981a8ce130972de08d" :answer-field/choices ["q-130996/selection/1ef83273bf8719dd6db6c440e0c0e3d9d136bdf66ea3f4f6db78210e7aebfed3" "q-130996/selection/b073349d38b9807332f930743cc5ce844707509ff0ef625bc61514b80924c235" "q-130996/selection/1583ad1c235afa6d610408beccb6b8d503778c5e2df64a981a8ce130972de08d" "q-130996/selection/491523a3d62207c0b47e9c957e7ca9e1c64ef62097cde0d6985d20945c91f2da" "q-130996/selection/b34d76d1c0f1ddc92081e1f2abec37a147c832448b1ac795ea8045da7d2b1097"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130996" :question/id #uuid "69f670aa-e26f-55f5-ae96-ac7b02fbdf63" :question/math-academy-id "q-130996" :question/problem "For the differential equation $x{y}^{″}+(x+1){y}^{′}-y=x{e}^{x},$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\nx{y}^{″}+(x+1){y}^{′}-y=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130996/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66ec8603-ae96-5212-88e1-4571d7face6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130996"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64963"] :question/problem "For the differential equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y={x}^{3},$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-93781/selection/00fe80f7699fcb891e4a1209a851ba86462600824ca07c9d11ff06d654a476f3" :answer/id #uuid "baac910b-772d-5934-afdb-6bf36a05c9fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+\\frac{6}{x-1}{y}^{′}=\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{(x-1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93781/selection/a7c961e5fd030cf12ef20f4bbf4439b47a8276fb58321932c4043552b4946f69" :answer/id #uuid "b591dd7e-67bc-592a-9483-208f99afb88f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}{y}^{″}+(x-1){y}^{′}=2{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93781/selection/1459daf68eab88d227195228ea40a7aadc41c81c00bf9c999d0227c6217c5ef7" :answer/id #uuid "99a69dc3-b54c-533d-8221-a15e7983bb73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+\\frac{6}{x-1}{y}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93781/selection/b70becdd9907c91a9b00ac6ac919a26fa5504dac83f9a47d6e87de32328427fd" :answer/id #uuid "ea44105b-4a82-59bf-9a98-c0da46d76a94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}{y}^{″}+(x-1){y}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93781/selection/73431ab502c215e1ffadb7669c0df0d03d4613e0334a05fbd48341eff87990c3" :answer/id #uuid "97bca613-204d-5a0c-93f2-f9e89b5996a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}{y}^{″}+6(x-1){y}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93781/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a4b8892-e3f3-56ae-b719-37bd077420e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93781/selection/73431ab502c215e1ffadb7669c0df0d03d4613e0334a05fbd48341eff87990c3" :answer-field/choices ["q-93781/selection/00fe80f7699fcb891e4a1209a851ba86462600824ca07c9d11ff06d654a476f3" "q-93781/selection/a7c961e5fd030cf12ef20f4bbf4439b47a8276fb58321932c4043552b4946f69" "q-93781/selection/1459daf68eab88d227195228ea40a7aadc41c81c00bf9c999d0227c6217c5ef7" "q-93781/selection/b70becdd9907c91a9b00ac6ac919a26fa5504dac83f9a47d6e87de32328427fd" "q-93781/selection/73431ab502c215e1ffadb7669c0df0d03d4613e0334a05fbd48341eff87990c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93781" :question/id #uuid "aeba1546-0b0b-5f1d-9ecb-30a8dfd77cc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-93781" :question/problem "For the differential equation $(x-1)^{2}{y}^{″}+6(x-1){y}^{′}=2{x}^{3},$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n(x-1)^{2}{y}^{″}+6(x-1){y}^{′}=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93781/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66ec8603-ae96-5212-88e1-4571d7face6b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93781"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-65017"] :question/problem "For the differential equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+3y={e}^{x},$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+3y=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-338531/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "549a6203-d92c-550d-a36f-ac104a959412" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338531/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "4235cb7f-d7df-51e9-8750-f84e61256173" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338531/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "910c7651-00de-59a3-8211-956e290418f7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338531/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "730c36c7-13a2-5cad-a295-55c0003c22f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338531/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "42e753f1-9f0b-54c5-af3b-00b78018e7c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338531/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8bb9631-31f8-57b4-8dbf-afa49adc64d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-338531/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-338531/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-338531/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-338531/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-338531/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-338531/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338531" :question/id #uuid "79dba891-0fd5-5b33-acae-cf1ca4fcb237" :question/math-academy-id "q-338531" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\n- ${y}^{″}-3{y}^{′}+y={e}^{x},\\,y(0)=1,\\,y(2)=0$\n- ${y}^{″}+4y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-1$\n- ${y}^{″}-y={x}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=2$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The second system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$).\n\n- The third system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338531/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d0a7ede-b896-56c6-9b60-a6aec8eff9e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338531"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339256/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "188e19b8-04d9-5024-a1a0-560681b52a11" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339256/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "3557fe35-3d8a-5b9f-8319-034a0b55e292" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339256/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "f1ec3ff9-a194-5b32-b7b0-91f6b59a11e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339256/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "7c29f87b-9169-55a0-9fcd-db3d482e3a30" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339256/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "5c65fb1c-74b3-5c07-a63e-9a134cc05155" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339256/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "75cf2381-7b48-5325-b87b-78fc4e994f54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339256/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d34